"""Readable scientific report with exact local results and explicit claim limits."""
import html,json
from pathlib import Path
HERE=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;OUT=HERE/'results'
def e(s):return html.escape(str(s))
def table(headers,rows):
 return '<table><thead><tr>'+''.join('<th>'+e(h)+'</th>' for h in headers)+'</tr></thead><tbody>'+''.join('<tr>'+''.join('<td>'+str(c)+'</td>' for c in row)+'</tr>' for row in rows)+'</tbody></table>'
def effect(s):return f"{s['mean']:+.3f} [{s['ci95'][0]:+.3f}, {s['ci95'][1]:+.3f}]"
def rate(s):
 text=f"{s.get('successes',round(s['mean']*s['n']))}/{s['n']} ({100*s['mean']:.1f}%)"
 if 'wilson95' in s:text+=f"; Wilson [{100*s['wilson95'][0]:.0f}, {100*s['wilson95'][1]:.0f}]%"
 return text

def main():
 s=json.loads((OUT/'summary.json').read_text());t=json.loads((OUT/'theory_check.json').read_text())
 adaptive=json.loads((OUT/'adaptive_prompt/summary.json').read_text())
 facts=[json.loads(l) for l in (OUT/'facts.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
 anatomy=[json.loads(l) for l in (OUT/'anatomy.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
 gens=[json.loads(l) for l in (OUT/'generations.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
 gens += [json.loads(l) for l in (OUT/'adaptive_prompt/generations.jsonl').read_text().splitlines()]
 verdict=json.loads((OUT/'conclusions.json').read_text()) if (OUT/'conclusions.json').exists() else {'summary':'Analysis complete. See individual tests below.'}
 body='<h1>Reassessing the image–text information gap</h1><p>Follow-up to <code>med_mllm_gap_notes.pdf</code> · October 19, 2026 · Frozen HuatuoGPT-Vision-7B and MedSIGHT-Comp</p>'
 body+='<p class="lead">'+e(verdict['summary'])+'</p>'
 body+='<p>This report separates <b>missing-context attribution</b>, <b>visual information use</b>, and <b>representation availability</b>. It does not assume that low image sensitivity identifies which one failed. All source data and model weights were left unchanged.</p>'
 body+='<img class="plot" src="followup_results.png" alt="Source availability effects, missing-fact abstention and visual anatomy control"/>'
 body+='<h2>What changes in the interpretation of the first pilot?</h2><p>The prior 96-record experiment found smaller image-identity gains and larger caption gains in a heuristically selected external-context group. That is evidence of different model dependencies, not an estimate of the prevalence of unsupported supervision. Providing a caption can reveal the exact answer; age and history should legitimately depend on text when text is available. Prefix dependence also failed to separate the groups.</p><p>Further inspection found noisy controls: some visual-description targets are generic explanations or broad normality assertions; recorded CT/brain metadata sometimes describe radiographs, PET, neck images or histology montages. These issues weaken a comparison framed as verified visual versus nonvisual claims. The original artifacts remain untouched. This follow-up reuses the 12 previously reviewed explicit facts and separately checks 12 obvious CT head/chest examples visually. These are assistant structural labels, not expert clinical adjudication.</p>'
 body+='<h2>Prospective questions and experimental design</h2>'
 body+=table(['Hypothesis','Test performed','What it can establish'],[
 ['H1: Part of the target depends on missing context','For 12 original targets, score six context variants × correct/swap/no image. Compare retained imaging description with the identical description plus a paraphrased fact, and positive versus contradictory fact.','Dependence on supplied factual content beyond verbatim source copying. Still not evidence sufficiency or a Shannon-information estimate.'],
 ['H2: Attribution behavior can change without weight updates','For 12 facts, cross missing/positive/negative context × correct/swap/no image × baseline/provenance prompt × all six option orders. Score yes/no/unknown labels. Also generate natural answers when context is missing.','Availability-sensitive abstention and context updating under this prompt/task; no claim about clinical reliability.'],
 ['H3: A valid image-supported target can conflict with a textual prior','Use six head/chest CT pairs, holding question and unverified note fixed while swapping the actual image. Test neutral/head/chest note × image/no image × two policies × six option orders.','Coarse anatomical evidence use, joint pair correctness, and susceptibility to a misleading text label. This is not a lesion-removal test.'],
 ['H4: A frozen representation may retain a feature that a decoder can use','Extract selected encoder features, projector output, and image-token/last-prompt-token states at four LLM depths; perform leave-one-out cosine 1-nearest-neighbor classification.','An oracle-ladder pipeline sanity check on broad anatomy with a labeled reference gallery; no fitted probe and no conclusion about small lesions or unreported content.']])
 body+='<p>The selection, hypotheses and expected counts were saved in <a href="protocol.json">protocol.json</a> before the successful runs. Each model produced 216 target scores, 1,296 factual-choice evaluations, 864 anatomy-choice evaluations, 12 feature archives and 24 generated responses. Total: <b>4,752 scored prompt evaluations, 24 feature extractions, and 48 generations</b>. Each choice evaluation scores all three A/B/C tokens in one forward pass; candidate probabilities are normalized within those options only.</p>'
 body+='<h2>H1: Source availability versus verbatim copying</h2><p>Report the original target factual-span log probabilities, with earlier target tokens still teacher-forced. The six context variants are no context, original caption, retained imaging description, imaging description plus a positive paraphrase, the same description plus a contradictory paraphrase, and donor caption. “Retained imaging description” is a manually condensed paraphrase, not a guaranteed sufficient or exhaustive visual oracle. Thus original-caption removal also changes wording and length. The positive-versus-negative pair and the positive-versus-identical-description pair are the cleaner tests.</p>'
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for k in ['original_caption_gain','original_minus_visual_only','positive_paraphrase_minus_visual_only','positive_minus_negative_paraphrase','image_identity_without_context','image_identity_with_positive_context']:
   rr.append([model,k.replace('_',' '),effect(m['ladder']['fact_logp'][k]),effect(m['ladder']['mean_logp'][k])])
 body+=table(['Model','Paired contrast','Fact span: nats/token [bootstrap 95%]','Whole sentence: nats/token [95%]'],rr)
 body+='<p>Positive source dependence is appropriate for nonvisual facts when the source is supplied. The defect of interest is asserting the same fact as established when its source is absent. Neither a context gain nor an image gain by itself measures that defect. These 12 claims were reused from prior review; they are not a random population sample.</p>'
 body+='<h2>H2: Missing-fact abstention and context updating</h2><p>For each record, average the six order-specific normalized candidate probability vectors, then take the highest-probability semantic answer. “Correct” means unknown when the fact is absent, yes under its positive paraphrase, and no under its explicit contradiction. Missing-context questions deliberately name the proposition, so this is a challenging prompted-fact audit rather than an open-report hallucination rate.</p>'
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for g in m['choice_groups']:
   if g['task']=='fact' and g['image']=='correct':
    rr.append([model,g['policy'],g['context'],rate(g['accuracy']),f"{g['order_accuracy']['mean']:.3f}",f"{g['mean_option_mass']:.3f}"])
 body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Context','Aggregate choice correctness','Mean per-order accuracy','Raw mass on A/B/C'],rr)
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for g in m['fact_joint_context_update']:rr.append([model,g['policy'],g['image'],rate(g['accuracy'])])
 body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Image condition','Both positive and negative contexts correct'],rr)
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for g in m['policy_effects']:
   if g['task']=='fact':rr.append([model,g['context'],effect(g['probability_difference']),effect(g['accuracy_difference'])])
 body+=table(['Model','Context','Provenance − baseline: expected-option probability','Paired aggregate accuracy difference'],rr)
 body+='<p>Option probabilities are task-relative scores, not calibrated confidence. When A/B/C has low raw vocabulary mass, the forced-choice prediction may be far from the model’s natural first token. This is particularly relevant for reasoning-style answers; all raw masses and permutations are retained. A model can appear safe when “unknown” is offered and still assert facts in natural generation.</p>'
 body+='<h2>H3: Does the image control an obvious visual answer?</h2>'
 body+='<p><a href="selected_anatomy.jpg">Inspect all twelve selected CT figures and their anatomy labels</a>.</p>'
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for g in m['anatomy_regimes']:rr.append([model,g['policy'],g['regime'],rate(g['accuracy']),f"{g['order_accuracy']['mean']:.3f}"])
 body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Note relative to image','Anatomy accuracy','Mean per-order accuracy'],rr)
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for g in m['anatomy_pairs']:rr.append([model,g['policy'],g['context'],rate(g['joint_accuracy'])])
 body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Fixed text note','Both images in head/chest pair correct'],rr)
 body+='<p>A fixed-context pair requires answering head for the head CT and chest for the chest CT under the same note. A text-only predictor cannot get both right with the identical prompt. Because the change is broad anatomy rather than a subtle lesion, success is a positive control for visual use, not evidence that clinical findings override contextual priors. These six pairs do not validate counterfactual lesion edits.</p>'
 body+='<h2>Adaptive robustness check: does a second prompt resolve the tradeoff?</h2><p>The original caution prompt improved missing-fact abstention, but Huatuo answered unknown on 10/12 explicitly negative patient records. MedSIGHT answered unknown on 11/12 clear anatomy images paired with a misleading note. Those are failures to use supplied evidence. The original results are retained; a second prompt was designed after observing them and evaluated on every original case, without exclusions.</p><p>The second factual instruction explicitly distinguishes supported, contradicted and undetermined statements. Its visual instruction asks for a specific anatomical answer when the image is clear, even if the note disagrees. This is an adaptive sensitivity analysis on the same records, not held-out prompt validation. It adds 2,160 scored choice prompts and 24 generations. Across both stages: <b>6,912 scored prompt evaluations, 24 feature extractions and 72 generations</b>.</p>'
 body+='<img class="plot" src="prompt_tradeoffs.png" alt="Prompt changes trade off missing-fact abstention, negative-evidence acceptance and visual evidence use"/>'
 rr=[]
 for model,m in adaptive['models'].items():
  for pol in ['baseline','provenance','evidence_first']:
   ff={r['context']:r for r in m['fact'] if r['policy']==pol}
   aa=next(r for r in m['anatomy'] if r['policy']==pol and r['regime']=='conflicting')
   rr.append([model,pol,rate(ff['missing']['accuracy']),rate(ff['positive']['accuracy']),rate(ff['negative']['accuracy']),rate(aa['accuracy'])])
 body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Missing fact: unknown','Positive fact: yes','Negative fact: no','Image beats wrong note'],rr)
 body+='<p>The evidence-first prompt largely repairs Huatuo’s negative-evidence response (2/12 to 11/12) while preserving missing-fact abstention. For MedSIGHT it restores conflicting-note anatomy accuracy (1/12 to 11/12) but reduces missing-fact abstention (12/12 to 5/12). There is no robust universal prompting fix here. All three requirements need to be tested together.</p>'
 rr=[]
 for model,m in adaptive['models'].items():
  for r in m['no_image']:rr.append([model,r['policy'],r['context'],r['prediction']])
 body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Text note, but no image supplied','Predicted answer (expected unknown)'],rr)
 body+='<p>Each no-image anatomy row is a <b>single distinct control prompt</b> repeated across the twelve record IDs; those repeats are not independent trials. No binomial or bootstrap interval is interpreted for this control. The evidence-first instruction makes both models choose a body region even with no image, illustrating why a visual-answer success alone does not validate evidence availability checking. Primary numerical files retain the repeated-record descriptive summaries for traceability.</p>'
 body+='<p>Natural generation further limits the forced-choice conclusion. Under the original caution prompt, Huatuo changes a biopsy claim from “confirmed” to “not confirmed” instead of admitting that the test history is unavailable. MedSIGHT sometimes claims that an absent patient record establishes the answer. These are concrete reasons to audit the content of abstaining answers and to keep explicit negative evidence separate from missing evidence. All 72 responses are listed below; they are not independently clinician-scored.</p>'
 body+='<p>See <a href="adaptive_prompt/protocol.json">the adaptive protocol</a>, <a href="adaptive_prompt/summary.json">all adaptive summaries</a> and <a href="prompt_tradeoffs.pdf">the exportable prompt comparison figure</a>.</p>'
 body+='<h2>H4: Frozen feature retrieval across layers</h2><p>The feature prompt is identical for every image: “Describe the supplied image briefly.” No anatomy labels, source captions, target answers or clinical histories enter extraction. Encoder features are captured immediately before the multimodal projector, corresponding to the selected vision features actually sent downstream. Mean image-token states and the final prompt-token state are saved separately at roughly one-quarter, one-half, three-quarter and final LLM depth.</p>'
 rr=[]
 for model,m in s['models'].items():
  for g in m['features']:rr.append([model,g['layer'],f"{g['correct']}/{g['n']}",f"{g['permutation_p']:.4f}",g['dimension']])
 body+=table(['Model','Representation','LOO 1-NN accuracy','Exact balanced-label permutation p','Dimensions'],rr)
 body+='<p>Both models answer all baseline anatomy questions correctly, yet some middle-layer last-prompt-token retrieval scores are poor (Huatuo layer 14: 2/12), while image-token pooling at the same depth retrieves 11/12. Task wording and readout matter: this is a concrete warning against equating a failed probe with lost information. It does not establish where lesion information resides.</p>'
 body+='<p>The null enumerates all 924 assignments of six head labels to twelve examples, using fixed nearest-neighbor indices. No probe fitting or hyperparameter tuning occurs. The gallery still supplies labels; this is not zero-label recognition. There are only 12 figures, no patient-level split, and anatomy may correlate with montage layout, CT window and acquisition style. Positive retrieval does not prove that the LLM uses the feature; weak retrieval does not prove that it is absent. This is consistent with the broader caution in <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/1909.03368">Hewitt and Liang’s probe-control work</a>.</p>'
 body+='<h2>Theory: what is valid, and what needs revision?</h2><ol><li><b>The decomposition is an identity under the right assumptions.</b> For deterministic Z=g(I), finite variables and a specified joint distribution, H(Y|Z)=H(Y|I,C)+I(Y;C|I)+I(Y;I|Z). Add the conditional KL to obtain cross entropy. If question Q is supplied, condition the entire identity consistently on Q; if the encoder consumes context, revise the variables and Markov assumptions accordingly.</li><li><b>Ablation is not an entropy estimator.</b> Our fixed-model contrasts can reflect misspecification, input-distribution shift, wording, or copying. The <a href="https://proceedings.mlr.press/v162/ethayarajh22a.html">PVI methodology</a> defines a predictor family and fits/evaluates input and null-input predictors. Calling one frozen model’s ablation a measured Venn region is too strong. <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2002.10689">V-usable information</a> can increase through computation and therefore cannot simply replace Shannon MI in a decomposition based on data processing.</li><li><b>The pre/post boundary is a frozen-information boundary.</b> A decoder restricted to fixed Z cannot recover information absent from Z. Post-training that updates the encoder/projector, changes resolution or adds views can change Z; the impossibility does not apply unchanged. “Only pretraining closes coverage” should be a hypothesis about a specified frozen-backbone intervention, not a theorem about training chronology.</li><li><b>Missing direct supervision is not literally zero gradient.</b> Unmentioned anatomy can receive indirect signal through correlated labels, other examples, pretraining or auxiliary losses. Coverage should be defined against independently labeled visual findings, not inferred from report silence alone.</li><li><b>Fano needs a valid entropy lower bound.</b> With natural logarithms the simple bound uses ln(2), not 1: Pe ≥ max(0, [H(Y|Z)−ln(2)]/ln(K)). A model’s cross entropy upper-bounds H(Y|Z); inserting that upper bound into Fano does not give a valid error lower bound. The displayed loose bound is trivial for binary Y; the inverse-binary-entropy form is more informative when H is known.</li><li><b>Conformal remains a separate calibration claim.</b> <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2208.02814">Conformal risk control</a> needs the appropriate loss and exchangeable calibration/evaluation setup. <a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2402.10978">Conformal factuality</a> relies on factuality labels and a valid filtering construction. A novel gap score can affect efficiency; it does not eliminate these requirements. None of the current heuristic or assistant labels validates clinical guarantees.</li></ol>'
 body+='<h3>Exact numerical counterexample</h3><p>'+e(t['distribution'])+'</p>'
 body+=table(['Quantity','Nats'],[[k,f'{v:.6f}'] for k,v in t['terms'].items()]+[['Cross entropy',f"{t['cross_entropy']:.6f}"],['Sum residual',f"{t['decomposition_residual']:.2g}"],['True image mutual information',f"{t['true_image_mutual_information']:.6f}"],['Frozen image-ablation gain',f"{t['fixed_predictor_image_ablation_gain']:.6f}"]])
 body+='<p>The predictor overtrusts Z and assigns probability 0.9 to Y=Z, while its no-image output is uniform. Despite positive true image information, the ablation gain is negative. This exact counterexample validates the algebra and refutes identifying a fixed-model gain with the Shannon image-information term. Code and distribution are in <a href="theory_check.json">theory_check.json</a>.</p>'
 body+='<h2>Revised research priorities</h2><p>Use a <b>provenance × evidence-availability × counterfactual-consistency matrix</b> as the preliminary contribution. A good model should use history/pathology when supplied, avoid claiming those facts when missing, and change visual answers when the finding changes. A single image-PVI threshold cannot encode all three behaviors.</p>'
 body+=table(['Next experiment','Independent evidence needed','Decisive result'],[
 ['Finding-level oracle ladder','A small independently labeled lesion-present/absent set, masks or locations, and held-out patients; keep anatomy/acquisition matched.','Compare actual lesion labels across encoder/projector/LLM probes and behavior. If decodable yet unused, test causal localization or activation interventions before asserting a use gap.'],
 ['Coverage test','Expert labels for findings absent from report text, plus matched reported findings of comparable size and difficulty.','Compare recognition and feature decodability while controlling prevalence, lesion size and acquisition; report silence alone is insufficient.'],
 ['Mismatch versus redundancy','Separate context-derived facts from independently supported but prior-predictable visual findings.','Missing context should trigger uncertainty; supported rare-in-context visual findings should override priors. Avoid a uniform image-amplification objective.'],
 ['Original/source-caption versus independent evidence','Independent history/pathology snippets paraphrased by a blinded annotator, with unrelated and contradictory context controls.','A context gain persists without literal target overlap, and availability governs assertion/abstention.'],
 ['Source comparison','A common finding vocabulary, matched task and label uncertainty across corpora, with common models and input conventions.','Compare independently grounded claim rates and coverage; raw per-token likelihood distributions across COCO and medical reports are not comparable groundedness ratios.'],
 ['Intervention comparison','Fixed-encoder post-training versus encoder/projector-updating alignment with matched data and compute.','Only this can test where training changes are needed. Current frozen observational probes cannot settle it.']])
 body+='<h2>Natural-generation audit trail</h2><p>These are greedy outputs to direct fact questions with missing context, capped at 64 tokens. The cap is marked. They are qualitative examples, not a clinically adjudicated hallucination-rate estimate. Questions often name a diagnosis or history, which may prime agreement. Prompted abstention can be surface compliance; the positive/negative evidence conditions and visual controls therefore remain essential. The prompts and captured responses are in <a href="generations.jsonl">primary generations</a> and <a href="adaptive_prompt/generations.jsonl">adaptive generations</a>.</p>'
 for r in facts:
  body+='<details><summary>'+e(r['id']+' — '+r['fact_question'])+'</summary>'
  body+=table(['Model','Prompt','Output'],[[e(g['model']),e(g['policy']),e(g['answer'])+(' <b>[64-token cap]</b>' if g['truncated'] else '')] for g in gens if g['id']==r['id']])+'</details>'
 body+='<h2>All annotations and context interventions</h2>'
 for r in facts:
  body+='<details><summary>'+e(r['id']+' — '+r['claim'])+'</summary>'+table(['Field','Text'],[[e(k),e(r[k])] for k in ['question','target','caption','visual_context','positive','negative','fact_question']])+'</details>'
 body+='<h2>Reproducibility and limits</h2><p>Use <a href="../run_all.sh">run_all.sh</a> from the experiment directory. Models use the existing MedProbe native adapters in separate processes with BF16 inference. Score masks and target lengths are asserted; native-forward cross-entropy and choice log-probabilities are checked. Greedy decoding uses the underlying Qwen core because the installed Transformers version passes an unsupported cache_position argument to Huatuo’s legacy generation wrapper. Cached continuation is checked against full-prefix decoding. Early wrapper-check outputs are archived under development_wrapper_check and excluded.</p><p>All bootstrap effects resample records, never the six permutations independently (5,000 replicates; paired differences). Binary accuracy tables use Wilson intervals to avoid degenerate 100%-accuracy bootstrap intervals. Pair metrics resample the six image pairs. Intervals are exploratory, unadjusted for multiple comparisons, and do not generalize beyond these convenience samples. Feature p-values test label exchangeability conditional on fixed similarities, not clinical causality. Corpus-derived cases may have been seen during training. There is no held-out clinical benchmark, no training intervention, no model ranking, no adjudicated mismatch prevalence, no measured scaling effect, and no demonstrated conformal guarantee.</p>'
 body+='<p>Artifacts: <a href="summary.json">all numerical summaries</a> · <a href="choice_records.jsonl">order-aggregated choices</a> · <a href="ladder_contrasts.csv">paired target contrasts</a> · <a href="facts.jsonl">fact manifest</a> · <a href="anatomy.jsonl">anatomy manifest</a> · <a href="followup_results.pdf">exportable figure</a> · <a href="huatuo.meta.json">Huatuo provenance</a> · <a href="medsight.meta.json">MedSIGHT provenance</a></p>'
 css='body{font:16px/1.55 system-ui,sans-serif;max-width:1250px;margin:40px auto;padding:0 24px;color:#17212b}h1,h2,h3{line-height:1.2}h2{margin-top:2.3em}table{border-collapse:collapse;width:100%;font-size:14px;margin:20px 0}th,td{border:1px solid #d5dce3;padding:9px;text-align:left;vertical-align:top}th{background:#edf2f6}tr:nth-child(even){background:#fafbfd}.lead{font-size:20px;border-left:5px solid #2166ac;padding-left:16px}.plot{width:100%}details{padding:10px;border:1px solid #d5dce3;margin:8px 0}summary{cursor:pointer}code{font-size:.9em}li{margin:12px 0}a{color:#155d9d}'
 (OUT/'report.html').write_text('<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Medical MLLM information gap: follow-up pilot</title><style>'+css+'</style><body>'+body+'</body></html>')
 print(OUT/'report.html')
if __name__=='__main__':main()
